From 71c521dbd0bd3f7aad2ba917fc335cedd94513e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Mausberg <samuelmausberg@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:33:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Certified LM head: fixed-noise sampled verify for EAGLE/MTP

Behind SGLANG_CERTIFIED_HEAD_SAMPLED_VERIFY (off by default), a separate
arm. The target verify graph also captures the certified Gumbel-max sampler
(CertifiedHead.gumbel_sample) under its own device flag; the stock head runs
only when neither the greedy nor the sampled flag holds. Before a replay the
host sets the sampled flag when every request is seeded
(--enable-deterministic-inference) and sampled with temperature only (no
top-k, top-p or min-p), with no logit adjustments, no rejection sampling and
not DFlash, and stages each verify row's seed, position and temperature in
static buffers.

eagle_sample then verifies with fixed noise: each verify row's token is
SGLang's seeded sampler (div_(T), softmax, log, multinomial_with_seed) applied
to that row's logits at its seed and position, which the certified sampler
returns without the logits (undecided rows run that sampler on the stock
logits). A draft token is accepted iff it equals the sample, and the sample
is emitted at the first mismatch or as the bonus. The output is equal in law
to target sampling and does not depend on the drafter; it is token-identical
to SGLang's seeded sampler applied to the verify pass's own logits, not to
plain decoding, and it replaces the stock rejection-sampling verify. In check
mode the stock seeded sampler runs on the same verify logits outside the
graph and differing rows are counted.
